  "server": "pnpm exec tsx src/index.ts --prod. The served UI is the compiled web build. Vite is not in this process tree.",
  "pages": "Real https://chatgpt.com loads. Recorded hostname chatgpt.com, loading false, on a fresh profile (signed-out page). Query strings were not recorded.",
  "method": "Three samples, one second apart, after each view count reported loading false. RSS is the sum of VmRSS from /proc/pid/status for every descendant, including processes whose smaps_rollup is unreadable. PSS is the sum of Pss from smaps_rollup only for processes where that file was readable. Electron main heap is process.memoryUsage() inside the Electron main process, sampled once after the three RSS samples. Backend V8 heap was not instrumented.",
  "accounting": "Summed RSS counts a shared page in every process that maps it. It is a resident-set total, and it is larger than unique memory. Partial PSS covers only processes with a readable smaps_rollup. That partial PSS stays near 216 MiB as ChatGPT views are added, while the unreadable sandboxed children hold the added resident memory. Publish RSS for the full tree. Publish PSS only with the count of excluded processes. Keep the Electron tree and the backend tree separate.",
  "classification": "Every Electron descendant is in the RSS sum. The chrome-sandbox child exposed --type=zygote. Other sandboxed children had a readable command line with no --type, so renderer, GPU, and utility roles are not assigned to individual PIDs. Processes with a null PSS are those sandboxed children. Their RSS is in smapsUnreadableRssKib.",
